-- title:
--   Randomized online scheduling algorithm
-- statement:
--   A **randomized online algorithm** on a measurable space $\Omega$ is a family $(\mathrm{ALG}_\omega)_{\omega\in\Omega}$ of deterministic online algorithms whose rates $(\omega,t)\mapsto r^{\omega}_j(t)$ are jointly measurable for every instance and job. With a probability measure on $\Omega$, the instance is fixed before $\omega$ is drawn: this is the oblivious adversary, which "does not see the random bits generated by the algorithm".
--
--   **Formalization Note** Joint measurability only excludes algorithms whose expected objective is undefined; with it, $\omega\mapsto f_J(\mathrm{ALG}_\omega(J))$ is measurable and bounded.
-- source:
--   Agrawal–Baruah–Kehne–Nirjhor–Rockwell–Wein, Scheduling Jobs to Maximize Minimum Fractional Completion, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 84f86375…80e0e), Section 1, pp.1 and 3 (PDF pp.3 and 5)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MaxMinFracSched_Job
import Definitions.Def_MaxMinFracSched_OnlineAlg

namespace MaxMinFracSched

/-- **A randomized online scheduling algorithm.** Agrawal–Baruah–Kehne–Nirjhor–Rockwell–Wein, *Scheduling Jobs to Maximize Minimum Fractional
Completion*, STOC 2027 submission manuscript (sha256 84f86375…80e0e), Section 1, p.1 (PDF p.3): "For randomized
schedulers, the expected competitive ratio is given by α = E[mini∈J fi]/f̂J", and p.3: "an
oblivious adversary is one that does not see the random bits generated by the algorithm."

A randomized online algorithm on the sample space `Ω` is a family of deterministic online
algorithms indexed by the random outcome `ω`, whose rates are jointly measurable in `(ω, t)`.
The instance is fixed before `ω` is drawn, which is the oblivious adversary.

**Formalization Note.** Joint measurability only excludes algorithms whose expected objective is
undefined; with it, `ω ↦ minFrac J ((alg ω).sched J)` is measurable and bounded. -/
structure RandOnlineAlg (Ω : Type*) [MeasurableSpace Ω] where
  /-- the deterministic online algorithm run on outcome `ω` -/
  alg : Ω → OnlineAlg
  /-- joint measurability of the rates in the outcome and the time -/
  meas : ∀ (J : Finset Job) (j : Job), Measurable (fun p : Ω × ℝ => (alg p.1).sched J j p.2)

end MaxMinFracSched


